# Godot 4 import cache and editor state.
#
# This is the single most important line in the file. `.godot/` holds the
# compiled/imported copies of every texture, mesh and HDRI in assets/ - on this
# project it is over 500 MB, more than twice the size of everything else
# combined. It is derived data: Godot rebuilds it the first time anyone opens
# the project, and a copy built on one machine is not reliably usable on
# another. It must never be committed.
.godot/

# Older Godot 3 name for the same thing, in case anyone opens this with 3.x.
.import/

# Exported builds
build/
export/
*.exe
*.pck
*.zip
*.apk
*.dmg

# Editor-local, per-user settings. Deliberately not shared: these hold window
# layouts and absolute paths from whoever's machine they came off.
*.translation
export_presets.cfg
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Screenshots and logs written by the test harness at runtime. The ones that
# belong in the repo live in docs/screenshots and are committed explicitly.
shots/
*.log
user://

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# NOTE: *.import files ARE committed on purpose.
# They are small text files holding each asset's import settings and stable
# resource UID. Without them, every teammate's Godot assigns different UIDs on
# first open and the scene files stop resolving - which is exactly the "it
# works on my machine" failure this project has to avoid.
